WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:01.250 --> 00:09.510
Effective presenters not only think about their words, not only pay attention to their physical presence and their vocal emphasis,

2
00:10.600 --> 00:19.750
they also pay attention to their audience, because really inspiring presenters will respond to what’s happening in the moment in the room.

3
00:20.520 --> 00:29.250
That ability to make an emotional connection is the third crucial element of style that brings your message alive.

4
00:30.090 --> 00:33.350
So what are some of the ways you can connect emotionally with an audience?

5
00:35.720 --> 00:40.320
First of all, look at them. Look them in the eye.

6
00:41.130 --> 00:44.670
Whether it’s a big audience or a small audience, make contact.

7
00:45.290 --> 00:51.140
Now, if you’re speaking to a convention with a thousand people in the room, of course you can’t make eye contact with all of them.

8
00:51.850 --> 00:57.630
But make eye contact with some individuals at the front. Let your gaze linger, and then move on.

9
00:58.210 --> 01:02.310
And also, just anything you can do verbally to express empathy.

10
01:02.950 --> 01:11.940
A simple thing like, “Okay, I know we’re all looking forward to lunch, but I just need you to concentrate for another 20 minutes.”

11
01:12.900 --> 01:15.970
Expressing empathy gets people on your side.

12
01:17.130 --> 01:23.490
Also, any time you open up a topic, tell people what you understand about how they feel about that topic now.

13
01:25.350 --> 01:31.040
So: “We’re going to talk about cost now. I know this is a painful topic. Nobody likes talking about it,

14
01:31.650 --> 01:37.030
but I really appreciate that you’ve given me some focused ideas to move forward with.

15
01:37.610 --> 01:44.000
And before we start, are there any thoughts you have, or concerns you have, about how we’re doing this?”

16
01:45.220 --> 01:51.910
So really kicking things off by putting them in the centre — that will build an emotional connection

17
01:52.230 --> 01:59.230
with your audience, or the people you’re in a meeting with. The other, deeper point is really about your ultimate state.

18
01:59.940 --> 02:06.880
Are you going into that meeting in an open state, with confidence and authenticity?

19
02:07.910 --> 02:15.810
If you are, people will connect with that. Always remember that any presentation, at its best, is a dialogue.

20
02:16.490 --> 02:23.390
That’s why the C of EPIC is conversation. It isn’t one-way communication. It’s two-way.

21
02:24.610 --> 02:31.680
And the starting point for that is the emotional connection you forge with the audience. Build your empathy with the audience,

22
02:32.130 --> 02:36.710
because if you don’t have empathy for them, they’re not going to connect with you.

